From b73d34ae7b6d8d937282313712f23fc9b8d73ceb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:15:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] IOP: run in batches at EE event boundaries (PCSX2's EEsCycle
 scheme)

Every recompiled backward-branch checkpoint (32 EE cycles) ran the IOP for
4 IOP cycles: a thread-map scan, timer service and a timeslice each time.
runEeCycles now banks EE cycles and the IOP runs when they reach its next
event (delayed-thread wake, DMA completion, CDVD callback, timer; 8 EE
cycles per IOP cycle), 3072 EE cycles (PCSX2 eeWaitCycles = iopWaitCycles
384 x 8), or before any EE call into the IOP (RPC, SIF transfer, IOP
memory, heap, bind poll, modules), which syncs it first. Calls that may
wake a thread or schedule an event reschedule the batch on return; a
timeslice inside a batch ends at the next event.

PS2X_IOP_BATCH=0 keeps the per-checkpoint stepping (A/B performance switch).
DebugSnapshot: emulatorEeBatching, emulatorRuns, emulatorPendingEeCycles.

Reference: PCSX2 v2.9.134 pcsx2/R5900.cpp _cpuEventTest_Shared,
pcsx2/R3000A.cpp PSX_INT, iopEventTest.

Tests: ps2_iop_batch_tests (fewer runs for the same cycles, event deadline,
EE calls sync first); ps2x PS2SifDma (sceSifSetDma syncs, PS2X_IOP_BATCH=0).
